.TH CYAML_DECLARE_SCOPED 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cyaml_declare_scoped \- declare a cyaml variable with automatic RAII destruction
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cyaml.h>

cyaml_declare_scoped(var_name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Declares a cyaml handle variable named var_name and attaches a GCC
cleanup attribute so that ___cyaml_destroy() is called automatically
when var_name goes out of scope.

The cleanup runs in reverse declaration order at the end of the
enclosing block, whether it exits normally, via break/continue/return,
or via goto.

This is a GCC/Clang extension; it is not available on MSVC.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
var_name  Name of the variable to declare.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
{
    cyaml_declare_scoped(doc) = cyaml_parse("x: 1\en", NULL);
    if (!doc) return;
    /* ... use doc ... */
}  /* doc is freed automatically here */
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_declare (3),
.BR cyaml_destroy (3),
.BR ___cyaml_destroy (3)
